{
  "$comment": "The sandbox images the apps offer (Cua Spaces, the OpenKoalaBots samples) and the docs list (os-image-catalog, generated by scripts/docs-generators/sandbox.ts). One source: edit here, then run `pnpm docs:generate:sandbox` in docs/ and `node samples/openkoalabot-example-swift/scripts/gen-images.mjs`. Canonical entries are checked against libs/cua/crates/cua-image/src/canonical.rs. Benchmark entries name their `lock` (the digests the bench publisher promoted; `python3 scripts/images/gen-image-constants.py` turns them into cua_bench/images.py) and the `benchmarks` they run. Every image ref elsewhere in the repo must be one of these, a lock pin, or an entry of scripts/images/image-refs-allowlist.json (scripts/images/check-image-refs.py). Pickers (the Spaces apps, the samples) and the image tables offer the entries with published=true whose group does not set `picker: false` (benchmark images are for cua-bench, not Spaces). `distro` names the guest: `id` (`ubuntu`, `omarchy`, `macos`, `windows`; it picks the OS icon) and `name`, the pretty name the apps show while a Space is created and until it reports its own. `arch` lists its platforms, `sdk` the SDK constructor that names it and `guide` its docs page. `browsers` lists the browsers the image ships; cua-driver browser tools (CDP) drive the Chromium-family ones when the image has cua-spacesd. `digest` (optional) is the published digest the moving tag was verified at. `sizes` (every entry with a digest) records, per platform, the bytes a pull downloads, what the pulled image takes on the host (`unpacked`) and the disk the Space sees (`disk`), measured at `sizes.digest` by `python3 scripts/images/record-image-sizes.py` (the release pipelines' `catalog` step; CI fails when it is stale). `tier` (canonical images) is `slim` (the minimum that passes `cua-spacesd doctor --strict` with every feature; CI and benchmarks use it), `full` (the default: slim plus dev tooling, no tag suffix) or `xcode` (macOS: full plus one pinned Xcode); the tag grammar is `<os-version>[-<tier>][-disk]`.",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "groups": [
    { "id": "canonical", "label": "Desktop images" },
    { "id": "benchmark", "label": "Adapter benchmark images", "picker": false },
    { "id": "distro", "label": "Distribution images" }
  ],
